    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n66608" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μεταγείτν-ιος</span></b> , ὁ,
		epith. of Apollo at Athens, <i><span class="en">
			Lysim.
			21
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Suid.
		</span></i>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μεταγειτνιών</span>
			:—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μεταγειτν-ιών</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῶνος</span>, ὁ, second month of the Attic year, <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				6.44
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				549a16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Publ.</u>
				14
			</span></i>; also at Delos, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				11(2).203
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>A</u>
				32
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>, and in Ionic cities, as Priene, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				278.2
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iv B. C.)</span>, Miletus, ib.<i><span class="en">
				633.75
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B. C.)</span>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πεδαγείτνιος</span>. (Derived by Gramm. from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετά, γείτων</span>, because people
				<i>changed their neighbours</i>: gen. sg. written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ</span></div>
